  <middle>
    <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">The <xref target="SORT" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="SORT"/> extension to the <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> protocol provides a means for the
server-based sorting of messages.  It defines a set of sort criteria
and the mechanism for determining the sort value of a message for
each such ordering.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2">The <xref target="SORT" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="SORT"/> FROM and TO orderings sort messages lexically on the
<xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> addr-mailbox of the first address in the message's From and To
headers, respectively.  This document provides two alternative
orderings, DISPLAYFROM and DISPLAYTO, which sort messages based on
the first From or To address's <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> addr-name (generally the same
as its <xref target="RFC5322" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5322"/> display-name), when present.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-3">A server that supports the full <xref target="SORT" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="SORT"/> extension as well as both the
DISPLAYFROM and DISPLAYTO sort criteria indicates this by returning
&quot;SORT=DISPLAY&quot; in its CAPABILITY response.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="conventions-used-in-this-document" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
      <name slugifiedName="name-conventions-used-in-this-document">Conventions Used in This Document</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-1">The key words &quot;<bcp14>MUST</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MUST NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>REQUIRED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL NOT</bcp14>&quot;,
&quot;<bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHOULD NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>RECOMMENDED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MAY</bcp14>&quot;, and &quot;<bcp14>OPTIONAL</bcp14>&quot; in this
document are to be interpreted as described in <xref target="RFC2119" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC2119"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="display-sort-value-for-an-address" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3">
      <name slugifiedName="name-display-sort-value-for-an-address">DISPLAY Sort Value for an Address</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-1">For the purposes of the sort criteria defined in this document, the
sort value for an <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> address structure is defined as follows:</t>
      <ul bare="false" empty="false" indent="3" spacing="normal" pn="section-3-2">
        <li pn="section-3-2.1">If the address structure's <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> addr-name is non-NIL, apply the
procedure from <xref target="RFC5255" section="4.6" sectionFormat="comma" format="default" derivedLink="https://rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5255#section-4.6" derivedContent="RFC5255"/>.  (That is, decode any
<xref target="RFC2047" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC2047"/> encoded-words and convert the resulting character string
into a charset valid for the currently active <xref target="RFC4790" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4790"/> collation,
with a default of UTF-8.)  If the resulting octet string is not
the empty string, use it as the sort value for the address.</li>
        <li pn="section-3-2.2">Otherwise, if the address structure's <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> addr-mailbox and
<xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> addr-host are both non-NIL, the sort value for the address
is addr-mailbox@addr-host.</li>
        <li pn="section-3-2.3">Otherwise, if the address structure's <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> addr-mailbox is non-NIL, the sort value for the address is its addr-mailbox.</li>
        <li pn="section-3-2.4">If none of the above conditions are met, the sort value for the
address is the empty string.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section anchor="the-displayfrom-and-displayto-sort-criteria" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4">
      <name slugifiedName="name-the-displayfrom-and-displayto-sort-criteria">The DISPLAYFROM and DISPLAYTO Sort Criteria</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-1">This document introduces two new <xref target="SORT" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="SORT"/> sort criteria, DISPLAYFROM
and DISPLAYTO.  A message's sort value under these orderings <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> be
derived as follows:</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-2">A &quot;derived-addr&quot; value is created from the <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> envelope structure
resulting from a FETCH ENVELOPE on the message.  For DISPLAYFROM, the
derived-addr value is the <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> env-from value.  For DISPLAYTO, the
derived-addr value is the <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> env-to value.</t>
      <ul bare="false" empty="false" indent="3" spacing="normal" pn="section-4-3">
        <li pn="section-4-3.1">If the derived-addr value is NIL, the message's sort value is the
empty string.</li>
        <li pn="section-4-3.2">Otherwise, the message's sort value is the DISPLAY sort value of
the first <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> address in the derived-addr value.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section anchor="formal-syntax" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-5">
      <name slugifiedName="name-formal-syntax">Formal Syntax</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-1">The following syntax specification uses the Augmented Backus-Naur
Form (ABNF) notation as specified in <xref target="RFC5234" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5234"/>.  <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> defines the
non-terminal &quot;capability&quot;, and <xref target="SORT" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="SORT"/> defines &quot;sort-key&quot;.</t>
      <sourcecode type="abnf" markers="false" pn="section-5-2"><![CDATA[
capability    =/ "SORT=DISPLAY"

sort-key      =/ "DISPLAYFROM" / "DISPLAYTO"
]]></sourcecode>
    </section>
    <section anchor="security-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-6">
      <name slugifiedName="name-security-considerations">Security Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-6-1">This document defines an additional IMAP4 capability.  As such, it
does not change the underlying security considerations of <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/>.
The author believes that no new security issues are introduced with
this additional IMAP4 capability.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="internationalization-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-7">
      <name slugifiedName="name-internationalization-considerations">Internationalization Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-7-1">DISPLAYFROM and DISPLAYTO are string-based sort criteria.  As stated
in <xref target="SORT" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="SORT"/>, the active <xref target="RFC4790" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4790"/> collation as per <xref target="RFC5255" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5255"/> <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> be
used when sorting such strings.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-7-2">The DISPLAYFROM and DISPLAYTO orderings sort on the full decoded
<xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> addr-name, when present.  They do not attempt to parse this
string in a locale- or language-dependent manner in order to
determine and sort on some semantically meaningful substring such as
the surname.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="iana-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-8">
      <name slugifiedName="name-iana-considerations">IANA Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-8-1"><xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/> capabilities are registered by publishing a Standards Track or
IESG-approved Experimental RFC.  This document constitutes
registration of the SORT=DISPLAY capability in the <xref target="IMAP" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="IMAP"/>
capabilities registry.</t>
    </section>
  </middle>
